From an indication to a defined gas measurement (@gas-measurement-entry: 0, is #chapter, #part-of @industrial-gases-and-vacuum, #source "../sources/Total-and-Partial-Pressure-Jousten.lingua#r_7SH9NGBWVVK5YN24S2VZPTW45M", #source "../sources/Ionization-Gauge-Calibration-Fedchak.lingua#r_18KG5KWT64MPYQ4D47V1T99CKW", #source "../sources/Gas-Flow-Standards-NIST.lingua#r_2FJV0VJ3K710PNV7E45JGGJXG5", #industrial-gases-and-vacuum "Mechanical-pressure-number-density-and-a-gas-state.lingua#r_4RCAWC3VWQFXSVW8Q1K34P22NJ") { r_4NFJD99T219WZK4XG65H258WHR
**Read in full:** [Total and Partial Pressure Measurement — Karl Jousten](../sources/Total-and-Partial-Pressure-Jousten.lingua#r_7SH9NGBWVVK5YN24S2VZPTW45M) and [Calibration of ionization vacuum gauges — Fedchak and colleagues](../sources/Ionization-Gauge-Calibration-Fedchak.lingua#r_18KG5KWT64MPYQ4D47V1T99CKW); then [Gas flow standards and their uncertainty — Wright and colleagues](../sources/Gas-Flow-Standards-NIST.lingua#r_2FJV0VJ3K710PNV7E45JGGJXG5) as flow methods are developed. Keep the shared metrology route available for uncertainty and inference.

Begin with the decision or physical question. Define pressure, amount flow, leak flow or composition at a location, under stated conditions and over a stated time interval. A number on a display is an indication; the measurement result includes the model and evidence connecting that indication to the quantity.

Follow the chain from gas to interaction, transducer, electrical signal, conversion and report. At each stage identify a possible dependence on gas species, temperature, geometry, history or time. The same indication can have different meanings under different operating states.

The earlier production, vacuum and delivery accounts supply the physical system being measured. Sampling is another part of that system: it can delay, transform or perturb the material. Portuguese terms include mensurando, indicação, calibração, rastreabilidade metrológica and incerteza.

**Work:** Rewrite three ambiguous claims—“the pressure is low,” “the line is leak-tight,” and “the gas is pure”—as measurable questions with quantities, conditions and a required distinction between competing outcomes. Carry one example through the calibration and research studies.

**Return:** [Industrial gases, vacuum and high-purity supplies — from molecules to useful service](../Industrial-gases-and-vacuum.lingua#r_3GHQJEYMYEN6JDKSF4PPJ403RF).
**Continue in gas and vacuum systems:** [Mechanical pressure, number density and a gas state](Mechanical-pressure-number-density-and-a-gas-state.lingua#r_4RCAWC3VWQFXSVW8Q1K34P22NJ).

